title Second search pass widens the Jiva Goswami bibliography with WebSearch
prompt Keaton asked to search other websites for the same content, after the first pass left twelve titles unconfirmed.
think Loaded WebSearch and targeted the four most likely-real gaps first: Locana-rocani, Durgama-sangamani, Priti Sandarbha, Krama Sandarbha -- rather than re-guessing archive.org IDs blind.
think Priti Sandarbha resolved immediately: archive.org identifier priti_sandarbha, same Haridas Shastri Hindi-translation series as the other five Sandarbhas already verified. Moved it into the verified table.
think Found sandarbhas.jiva.org ("The Sat Sandarbhas of Jiva Gosvami") via search -- a dedicated academic project site (trans. Satyanarayana Dasa) claiming Sanskrit text plus English translation for all six Sandarbhas. Root page fetched clean; every /book/<name>/ deep path the summarizing fetch proposed then 404'd on direct fetch, so recorded the root as live and the path shape as unconfirmed rather than trusting the first fetch's paraphrased nav.
think Searched the remaining gaps: found archive.org identifier GopalaTapaniTikaPuridas for Sukha-bodhini (moved to verified), and enough secondhand detail (Wikipedia's Sat Sandarbhas article, Vaniquotes, a 1932 Kavyamala print-edition description, commercial booksellers) to confirm Krama Sandarbha, Durgama-sangamani, and Locana-rocani are real, correctly-titled works -- without finding a free open-access digital text for any of the three. Filed these in a new middle tier rather than either the verified table or the unconfirmed list, since confirming a work's existence and finding a free copy are different claims.
think Caught a likely misattribution while searching Dana-keli-kaumudi-tika: every source names the well-known Mahati-tika on that play as Visvanatha Cakravarti's commentary, not Jiva's. Recorded this as a flag rather than silently keeping or silently dropping the original bibliography's claim.
think Also re-verified grantha.jiva.org's fetch block held even on a specific entry page found via search (?show=entry&e_no=722), so the 403 is a site-wide bot block rather than a root-only artifact.
obs Splitting "confirmed real work, no free text found" from "verified with a working link" and from "still unconfirmed" is a three-way distinction the first pass's binary verified/unconfirmed table could not hold -- a title backed by a Wikipedia article and commercial editions is a stronger claim than one found nowhere, even with no link to give a reader.
file shastra/README.md -- moved Priti Sandarbha and Sukha-bodhini into Verified with real archive.org identifiers; added a Confirmed-to-exist-no-free-text tier for Krama Sandarbha, Durgama-sangamani, Locana-rocani; flagged the Dana-keli-kaumudi-tika attribution as likely wrong; added sandarbhas.jiva.org to the repositories table with its fetch-confirmed and fetch-unconfirmed parts named separately
recommend check-in (either) -- six titles remain genuinely unconfirmed after two passes (Bhagavat-sandarbha-suci-patra, Dhatu-sangraha, Sutra-malika, Laghu Hari-namamrta-vyakarana, Gopala-virudavali, Madhava-mahotsava); closing that gap likely needs a human browse of grantha.jiva.org and sandarbhas.jiva.org rather than another automated search pass
